question G1's face width (15 → 17) moves its front face off the Front plane (z 0 → -1): the mate G1 along S1 holds it on that plane and cannot take a distance, so the gearbox needs building again. Build again as Reducer_12to1_r2? That makes a new part for G1 (Gear_m1.5_N17_r2), reuses 3 parts that have not changed and makes a new layout part and assembly (Reducer_12to1_r2_Layout and Reducer_12to1_r2.SLDASM). Nothing is overwritten, and Reducer_12to1.SLDASM stays as it is on disk, but it shares the 3 reused parts: a later Update SolidWorks that changes one of them changes Reducer_12to1.SLDASM too.
